# backplane-operator Sync Rule

When adding or changing files under `pkg/manager/manifests/` that affect hub-side
resources (not spoke agent templates under `manifests/templates/`), you MUST ALSO
update the corresponding templates in `stolostron/backplane-operator`:

  `pkg/templates/charts/toggle/hypershift/templates/`

Local path (if checked out): `/Users/yiraekim/Documents/GitHub/origin/backplane-operator/pkg/templates/charts/toggle/hypershift/templates/`

## Required syncs

### New hub-facing ports
→ Add `containerPort` entry to `hypershift-addon-manager-deployment.yaml`

```yaml
ports:
- containerPort: 8443
  name: hcp-proxy
  protocol: TCP
```

### New hub manager RBAC rules
→ Add rules to `hypershift-addon-manager_clusterrole.yaml`

Currently added for the HCP proxy:
```yaml
- apiGroups: ["clusterview.open-cluster-management.io"]
  resources: ["userpermissions"]
  verbs: ["list"]
- apiGroups: ["apiregistration.k8s.io"]
  resources: ["apiservices"]
  verbs: ["get", "list", "create", "update", "patch"]
- apiGroups: ["config.openshift.io"]
  resources: ["apiservers"]
  verbs: ["get", "list", "watch"]
```

Note: `rbac.yaml` in `pkg/manager/manifests/hcp-proxy/` must stay in sync with the backplane-operator clusterrole. Both must include the `config.openshift.io/apiservers` rule so the SecurityProfileWatcher and `FetchAPIServerTLSProfile` can read the cluster TLS profile at startup and at runtime.

### New hub ServiceAccount
→ Add entry to `hypershift-addon-manager-serviceaccount.yaml`

## Why
The hub manager pod (Deployment, ClusterRole, ServiceAccount) is defined in
`backplane-operator`, not in this repo. Resources applied at runtime by
`applyHCPProxyManifests()` (Service, APIService, RBAC bindings) are fine here,
but the Deployment containerPorts and ClusterRole rules must be pre-provisioned
by MCE at install time.

Upstream PR reference: https://github.com/stolostron/backplane-operator/tree/main/pkg/templates/charts/toggle/hypershift/templates
